// AN ENUM HOLDS 254 VARIANTS, NUMBERED 1 TO 254 (`@FR-L-Enum`: "Variants are numbered from 1: 0
// is the absent value (L-Null) and 255 is the null a write spells, so an enum holds at most 254
// variants").  The largest legal enum still stores in one byte, its first variant is 1 and its
// last is 254, and the last round-trips through a field and a vector element; a nullable field
// of it holds null apart from all 254.  The 255th is the sibling refusal cell.
//
// Values hand-computed: V1 → 1, V254 → 254, sizeof 1; a struct { e: LBig, f: LBig? } is 2.
//
// Cross-backend; `main` runs every cell so the leak gate reads the file.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; every cell answered as hand-computed on 18594597b,
//   interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the asserts.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the message prints the numbers.
// HOLDS: V254 is not read as the reserved null code 255.

enum LBig {
  V1,
  V2,
